<title>USA: Tobacco deal would require industry pay $368.5 billion.</title>
<headline>Tobacco deal would require industry pay $368.5 billion.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A landmark tobacco agreement would require cigarette companies to pay $368.5 billion over 25 years to compensate the states and smokers, and to fund programs to help people quit smoking, states attorneys general said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Not one of these tobacco companies has yet paid a penny to anyone, but in this agreement, they agree to pay $368.5 billion over 25 years and who knows how much beyond that to individual claimants, state governments, tobacco control, public education and smoking cessation programs, and other vital causes,&quot; Connecticut Attorney General Dick Blumenthal said in a statement.</p>
</text>
